<header><p class="st-kicker">nomadic confederation · Central Asia and the Steppe</p><h1 class="st-title">Hephthalite Empire</h1><p class="st-meta">450 CE – 560 CE (approx.) · capital Kunduz</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The 'White Huns' who ruled Bactria and Sogdiana for a century, killed a Persian king in battle and forced Sasanian Persia to pay them tribute.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hephthalites">Hephthalites</a> rose in the region of the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/greco-bactrian-kingdom">Bactria</a> in the mid-5th century, perhaps as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassal</a> people of the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/rouran-khaganate">Rouran</a>. They drove out the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/kidarite-kingdom">Kidarite Kingdom</a> and fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sasanian-empire">Sasanians</a>, defeating and capturing <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peroz-i">Peroz I</a> and then killing him in battle in 484.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>From their capital at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kunduz">Kunduz</a> they ruled a loose empire from <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-samarkand">Sogdiana</a> to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tarim-basin">Tarim</a> oases and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hindu-kush">Hindu Kush</a>, with Bactrian as the administrative language. Byzantine writer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/procopius">Procopius</a> called them 'White <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a>' and described them as more settled than other Huns, with a single king and laws. They held <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kavad-i">Kavad I's</a> Sasanian throne in their gift and collected tribute from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/persia">Persia</a>, and Sogdian cities prospered on trade.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>Between about 557 and 560 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-turkic-khaganate">Turkic Khaganate</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/istami">Istämi</a>, allied with the Sasanian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khosrow-i">Khosrow I</a>, crushed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hephthalites">Hephthalites</a> near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bukhara">Bukhara</a>. Their lands were divided along the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/oxus">Amu Darya</a>, and Hephthalite principalities survived in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tokharistan">Tokharistan</a> under Turkic rule, later the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/yabghus-of-tokharistan">Yabghus of Tokharistan</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="nomadic confederation, 450 CE – 560 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M18 74 V58 Q50 30 82 58 V74 Z"/><path d="M42 74 V60 H58 V74"/><path d="M30 50 L50 36 L70 50"/><path d="M50 36 V26"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">nomadic confederation</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Central Asia and the Steppe</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:68.66%;width:2.19%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>450 CE – 560 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>nomadic confederation</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>nomadic</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Kunduz</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Akhshunwar, Ghadfar</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Buddhism, Zoroastrianism, Manichaeism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Bactrian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, <a href="/countries/uzbekistan">Uzbekistan</a>, <a href="/countries/tajikistan">Tajikistan</a>, <a href="/countries/turkmenistan">Turkmenistan</a>, <a href="/countries/pakistan">Pakistan</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Hephthalites, White Huns, Hayatila</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=505&amp;focus=hephthalite-empire" aria-label="Hephthalite Empire on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="6409 854 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Hephthalite Empire lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-tie" d="M6729 1110L6679 1109M6729 1110L6820 913M6729 1110L6357 1235"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M6679 1109h0M6820 913h0M6357 1235h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M6729 1110h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M6729 1110h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Kunduz. <a href="/atlas?year=505&amp;focus=hephthalite-empire">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
